IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa2-part7-private-to-public.l4: Part 7 (Re-registration as a means of altering a company's status), the introductory
-- section and the route from private to public company, ss 89-96, lines 1109-1225 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no point of view.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seams taken as inputs: s 283 "special resolution" (coa7), s 626, s 643, s 648 (coa14), s 593 (coa13), s 279J and s 279K (coa6),
-- s 763 "the authorised minimum" (coa16), s 831 "net assets" and "undistributable reserves" (coa18), s 547 "called-up share capital" (coa13),
-- s 1161 and s 1159 "holding company", "subsidiary" (keel), s 4(1), s 4(2), s 3(1) (keel; plain BOOLEAN).
-- Every name that is not in coa-core.l4 begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Introductory (s 89)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 89 alteration of status` IS ONE OF
    `s 89(a) from a private company to a public company`
    `s 89(b) from a public company to a private company`
    `s 89(c) from a private limited company to an unlimited company`
    `s 89(d) from an unlimited private company to a limited company`
    `s 89(e) from a public company to an unlimited private company`

-- src:1111 | 89 Alteration of status by re-registration
-- src:1112 | A company may by re-registration under this Part alter its status—
-- src:1113 | (a) from a private company to a public company (see sections 90 to 96);
-- src:1114 | (b) from a public company to a private company (see sections 97 to 101);
-- src:1115 | (c) from a private limited company to an unlimited company (see sections 102 to 104);
-- src:1116 | (d) from an unlimited private company to a limited company (see sections 105 to 108);
-- src:1117 | (e) from a public company to an unlimited private company (see sections 109 to 111).
@ref s 89 Alteration of status by re-registration (src:1111-1117)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      alteration IS A `s 89 alteration of status`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 89 the company may by re-registration under Part 7 alter its status in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER alteration
    WHEN `s 89(a) from a private company to a public company` THEN
        IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) from a private company to a public company"
    WHEN `s 89(b) from a public company to a private company` THEN
        IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) from a public company to a private company"
    WHEN `s 89(c) from a private limited company to an unlimited company` THEN
        IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` AND `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) from a private limited company to an unlimited company"
    WHEN `s 89(d) from an unlimited private company to a limited company` THEN
        IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` AND NOT (`s 3(1) the company is a limited company`) THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(d) from an unlimited private company to a limited company"
    WHEN `s 89(e) from a public company to an unlimited private company` THEN
        IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) from a public company to an unlimited private company"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Private company becoming public (ss 90-96)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- A conjunction of MAYBE BOOLEAN answers that keeps "not covered": any JUST FALSE makes it JUST FALSE, otherwise any
-- NOTHING makes it NOTHING.
-- src:1119 | 90 Re-registration of private company as public
-- src:1120 | (1) A private company (whether limited or unlimited) may be re-registered as a public company limited by shares if—
-- src:1121 | (a) a special resolution that it should be so re-registered is passed,
-- src:1122 | (b) the conditions specified below are met, and
-- src:1123 | (c) an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 94, together with—
-- src:1124 | (i) the other documents required by that section, and
-- src:1125 | (ii) a statement of compliance.
@ref s 90(1) Re-registration of private company as public (the conditions together) (src:1119-1125)
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(1) all of the answers hold` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN answer YIELD answer EQUALS JUST FALSE) answers
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "if" that introduces the conditions of the calling section ("may be re-registered as a public company limited by shares if— (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c) ..."; "The conditions are— (a) ... (e)")
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN answer YIELD answer EQUALS NOTHING) answers
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer another section gives is not known
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1126 | (2) The conditions are—
-- src:1127 | (a) that the company has a share capital;
-- src:1128 | (b) that the requirements of section 91 are met as regards its share capital;
-- src:1129 | (c) that the requirements of section 92 are met as regards its net assets;
-- src:1130 | (d) if section 93 applies (recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration), that the requirements of that section are met; and
-- src:1131 | (e) that the company has not previously been re-registered as unlimited.
@ref s 90(2) The conditions (src:1126-1131)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 91 the requirements as to share capital are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 92 the requirements as to net assets are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 93(1) section 93 applies (recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 93(2) the requirements of section 93 are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(2) the conditions are met` MEANS
    `s 90(1) all of the answers hold`
        (LIST   (IF `the company has a share capital` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) -- (a) FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are— (a) that the company has a share capital"
              , `s 91 the requirements as to share capital are met` -- (b)
              , `s 92 the requirements as to net assets are met` -- (c)
              , `section 93 condition` -- (d)
              , (IF `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)) -- (e) FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that the company has not previously been re-registered as unlimited"
    WHERE
        `section 93 condition` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 93(1) section 93 applies (recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration)`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 93(2) the requirements of section 93 are met`
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- (d) "if section 93 applies": it does not, so the condition imposes nothing
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 93 applies is not known

-- src:1119 | 90 Re-registration of private company as public
-- src:1120 | (1) A private company (whether limited or unlimited) may be re-registered as a public company limited by shares if—
-- src:1121 | (a) a special resolution that it should be so re-registered is passed,
-- src:1122 | (b) the conditions specified below are met, and
-- src:1123 | (c) an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 94, together with—
-- src:1124 | (i) the other documents required by that section, and
-- src:1125 | (ii) a statement of compliance.
@ref s 90(1) Re-registration of private company as public (src:1119-1125)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 90(2) the conditions are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 94, together with the other documents required by that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of compliance is delivered together with the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(1) the private company may be re-registered as a public company limited by shares` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(1) the company is a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company (whether limited or unlimited) may be re-registered"
    ELSE
        `s 90(1) all of the answers hold`
            (LIST   `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`
                  , `s 90(2) the conditions are met`
                  , (IF `an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 94, together with the other documents required by that section` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
                  , (IF `a statement of compliance is delivered together with the application` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE))

-- src:1132 | (3) The company must make such changes—
-- src:1133 | (a) in its name, and
@ref s 90(3)(a) The company must change its name (src:1132-1133)
GIVEN `the company is being re-registered as a public company under section 90` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(3)(a) the company must make such changes in its name as are necessary in connection with its becoming a public company` MEANS
    IF `the company is being re-registered as a public company under section 90`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the company's "becoming a public company" on this re-registration

-- src:1132 | (3) The company must make such changes—
-- src:1134 | (b) in its articles,
-- src:1135 | as are necessary in connection with its becoming a public company.
@ref s 90(3)(b) The company must change its articles (src:1132-1135)
GIVEN `the company is being re-registered as a public company under section 90` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(3)(b) the company must make such changes in its articles as are necessary in connection with its becoming a public company` MEANS
    IF `the company is being re-registered as a public company under section 90`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the company's "becoming a public company" on this re-registration

-- src:1136 | (4) If the company is unlimited it must also make such changes in its articles as are necessary in connection with its becoming a company limited by shares.
@ref s 90(4) An unlimited company must also become a company limited by shares (src:1136-1136)
GIVEN `the company is being re-registered as a public company under section 90` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(4) the company must also make such changes in its articles as are necessary in connection with its becoming a company limited by shares` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is being re-registered as a public company under section 90`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the company's "becoming a company limited by shares" on this re-registration
    ELSE IF `the company is unlimited`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company is unlimited it must also make such changes in its articles"

-- ---- s 91: requirements as to share capital -----------------------------------------------------------

-- One allotment: shares allotted on the same terms.  The text speaks of "each of the company's allotted shares" (s 91(1)(b)),
-- so the requirements are applied allotment by allotment.
DECLARE `s 91 allotment` HAS
    `nominal value of the shares in the allotment` IS A NUMBER
    `amount paid up on those shares on account of their nominal value` IS A NUMBER
    `premium on those shares` IS A NUMBER
    `amount paid up on those shares on account of the premium` IS A NUMBER
    `date of the allotment` IS A DATE
    `allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid up by an undertaking that he or another should do work or perform services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that undertaking has been performed or otherwise discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `allotted otherwise than in cash, the consideration including an undertaking to the company other than one in paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the undertaking to the company has been performed or otherwise discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contract provides for the undertaking to be performed within five years from the time the special resolution is passed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1137 | 91 Requirements as to share capital
-- src:1138 | (1) The following requirements must be met at the time the special resolution is passed that the company should be re-registered as a public company—
-- src:1139 | (a) the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital must be not less than the authorised minimum;
@ref s 91(1)(a) The nominal value of the allotted share capital: not less than the authorised minimum (src:1137-1139)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital (shares disregarded under subsection (2) not counted: subsection (4))` IS A NUMBER
      `s 763 the authorised minimum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(1)(a) the nominal value of the allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum` MEANS
    IF `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital (shares disregarded under subsection (2) not counted: subsection (4))` AT LEAST `s 763 the authorised minimum`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital must be not less than the authorised minimum"

-- src:1137 | 91 Requirements as to share capital
-- src:1138 | (1) The following requirements must be met at the time the special resolution is passed that the company should be re-registered as a public company—
-- src:1140 | (b) each of the company's allotted shares must be paid up at least as to one-quarter of the nominal value of that share and the whole of any premium on it;
@ref s 91(1)(b) Each allotted share paid up at least one-quarter and the whole of any premium (src:1137-1140)
GIVEN a IS A `s 91 allotment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(1)(b) the allotment is paid up as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF       a's `amount paid up on those shares on account of their nominal value` AT LEAST (a's `nominal value of the shares in the allotment` DIVIDED BY 4)
         AND a's `amount paid up on those shares on account of the premium` AT LEAST a's `premium on those shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each of the company's allotted shares must be paid up at least as to one-quarter of the nominal value of that share and the whole of any premium on it"

-- src:1137 | 91 Requirements as to share capital
-- src:1138 | (1) The following requirements must be met at the time the special resolution is passed that the company should be re-registered as a public company—
-- src:1141 | (c) if any shares in the company or any premium on them have been fully or partly paid up by an undertaking given by any person that he or another should do work or perform services (whether for the company or any other person), the undertaking must have been performed or otherwise discharged;
@ref s 91(1)(c) An undertaking to do work or perform services must have been performed (src:1137-1141)
GIVEN a IS A `s 91 allotment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(1)(c) the allotment meets the paragraph` MEANS
    IF a's `paid up by an undertaking that he or another should do work or perform services`
    THEN IF a's `that undertaking has been performed or otherwise discharged`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the undertaking must have been performed or otherwise discharged"
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- the paragraph imposes nothing on shares not paid up by such an undertaking (fork 4: a requirement that is not engaged counts as met)

-- src:1137 | 91 Requirements as to share capital
-- src:1138 | (1) The following requirements must be met at the time the special resolution is passed that the company should be re-registered as a public company—
-- src:1142 | (d) if shares have been allotted as fully or partly paid up as to their nominal value or any premium on them otherwise than in cash, and the consideration for the allotment consists of or includes an undertaking to the company (other than one to which paragraph (c) applies), then either—
-- src:1143 | (i) the undertaking must have been performed or otherwise discharged, or
-- src:1144 | (ii) there must be a contract between the company and some person pursuant to which the undertaking is to be performed within five years from the time the special resolution is passed.
@ref s 91(1)(d) Another undertaking to the company: performed, or a contract for performance within five years (src:1137-1144)
GIVEN a IS A `s 91 allotment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(1)(d) the allotment meets the paragraph` MEANS
    IF a's `allotted otherwise than in cash, the consideration including an undertaking to the company other than one in paragraph (c)`
    THEN IF       a's `the undertaking to the company has been performed or otherwise discharged`
              OR  a's `a contract provides for the undertaking to be performed within five years from the time the special resolution is passed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then either— (i) the undertaking must have been performed or otherwise discharged, or (ii) there must be a contract ... within five years from the time the special resolution is passed"
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- the paragraph imposes nothing on shares not allotted in that way (fork 4)

-- src:1145 | (2) For the purpose of determining whether the requirements in subsection (1)(b), (c) and (d) are met, the following may be disregarded—
-- src:1146 | (a) shares allotted—
-- src:1147 | (i) before 22nd June 1982 in the case of a company then registered in Great Britain, or
-- src:1148 | (ii) before 31st December 1984 in the case of a company then registered in Northern Ireland;
@ref s 91(2)(a) Shares allotted before 22 June 1982 (Great Britain) or 31 December 1984 (Northern Ireland) (src:1145-1148)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      a IS A `s 91 allotment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(2)(a) the allotment may be disregarded` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN
        IF a's `date of the allotment` BELOW (Date 31 12 1984)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(ii) before 31st December 1984 in the case of a company then registered in Northern Ireland"
    OTHERWISE
        IF a's `date of the allotment` BELOW (Date 22 6 1982)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(i) before 22nd June 1982 in the case of a company then registered in Great Britain"

-- src:1145 | (2) For the purpose of determining whether the requirements in subsection (1)(b), (c) and (d) are met, the following may be disregarded—
-- src:1149 | (b) shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme by reason of which the company would, but for this subsection, be precluded under subsection (1)(b) (but not otherwise) from being re-registered as a public company.
@ref s 91(2)(b) Shares allotted under an employees' share scheme (src:1145-1149)
GIVEN a IS A `s 91 allotment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(2)(b) the allotment may be disregarded` MEANS
    IF       a's `allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme`
         AND `s 91(1)(b) the allotment is paid up as the paragraph requires` a EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST TRUE -- precluded under subsection (1)(b) "(but not otherwise)": only the (b) shortfall is disregarded
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme by reason of which the company would, but for this subsection, be precluded under subsection (1)(b) (but not otherwise)"

-- src:1150 | (3) No more than one-tenth of the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is to be disregarded under subsection (2)(a).
-- src:1151 | For this purpose the allotted share capital is treated as not including shares disregarded under subsection (2)(b).
@ref s 91(3) The most that may be disregarded under (2)(a): one-tenth of the allotted share capital (src:1150-1151)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital (not including shares disregarded under subsection (2)(b))` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the shares disregarded under subsection (2)(a)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(3) the disregard under subsection (2)(a) is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the nominal value of the shares disregarded under subsection (2)(a)` AT MOST (`the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital (not including shares disregarded under subsection (2)(b))` DIVIDED BY 10)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No more than one-tenth of the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is to be disregarded under subsection (2)(a)"

-- Paragraphs (b) to (d) over all the allotments, with the disregards of subsection (2) and the limit of subsection (3).
-- A share that fails and may be disregarded under (2)(b) (employees' share scheme, a (b) shortfall only) is excused;
-- one that fails and may be disregarded under (2)(a) is excused up to one-tenth of the allotted share capital.
-- src:1137 | 91 Requirements as to share capital
-- src:1138 | (1) The following requirements must be met at the time the special resolution is passed that the company should be re-registered as a public company—
-- src:1140 | (b) each of the company's allotted shares must be paid up at least as to one-quarter of the nominal value of that share and the whole of any premium on it;
-- src:1141 | (c) if any shares in the company or any premium on them have been fully or partly paid up by an undertaking given by any person that he or another should do work or perform services (whether for the company or any other person), the undertaking must have been performed or otherwise discharged;
-- src:1142 | (d) if shares have been allotted as fully or partly paid up as to their nominal value or any premium on them otherwise than in cash, and the consideration for the allotment consists of or includes an undertaking to the company (other than one to which paragraph (c) applies), then either—
-- src:1143 | (i) the undertaking must have been performed or otherwise discharged, or
-- src:1144 | (ii) there must be a contract between the company and some person pursuant to which the undertaking is to be performed within five years from the time the special resolution is passed.
@ref s 91(1) The requirements as to share capital (paragraphs (b) to (d)) (src:1137-1144)
GIVEN allotments IS A LIST OF `s 91 allotment`
      place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(1) the requirements of paragraphs (b) to (d) are met` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD `fails after subsection (2)(b)` a AND (NOT (`may be disregarded under subsection (2)(a)` a))) allotments
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following requirements must be met" ... "(b)", "(c)", "(d)": an allotment fails and cannot be disregarded
    ELSE IF `nominal value that needs the subsection (2)(a) disregard` AT MOST (`allotted share capital without the subsection (2)(b) shares` DIVIDED BY 10)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No more than one-tenth of the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is to be disregarded under subsection (2)(a)"
    WHERE
        `passes paragraphs (b), (c) and (d)` a MEANS
                `s 91(1)(b) the allotment is paid up as the paragraph requires` a EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 91(1)(c) the allotment meets the paragraph` a EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 91(1)(d) the allotment meets the paragraph` a EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `fails after subsection (2)(b)` a MEANS
                (NOT (`s 91(1)(c) the allotment meets the paragraph` a EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 91(1)(d) the allotment meets the paragraph` a EQUALS JUST TRUE))
            OR  (    `s 91(1)(b) the allotment is paid up as the paragraph requires` a EQUALS JUST FALSE
                 AND (NOT (`s 91(2)(b) the allotment may be disregarded` a EQUALS JUST TRUE)))
        `may be disregarded under subsection (2)(a)` a MEANS `s 91(2)(a) the allotment may be disregarded` place a EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `nominal value that needs the subsection (2)(a) disregard` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `nominal value of the shares in the allotment`)
                     (filter (GIVEN a YIELD `fails after subsection (2)(b)` a AND `may be disregarded under subsection (2)(a)` a) allotments))
        `allotted share capital without the subsection (2)(b) shares` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `nominal value of the shares in the allotment`) allotments)
            MINUS sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `nominal value of the shares in the allotment`)
                           (filter (GIVEN a YIELD `s 91(2)(b) the allotment may be disregarded` a EQUALS JUST TRUE) allotments))

-- src:1152 | (4) Shares disregarded under subsection (2) are treated as not forming part of the allotted share capital for the purposes of subsection (1)(a).
@ref s 91(4) Disregarded shares do not count towards the allotted share capital in paragraph (a) (src:1152-1152)
GIVEN allotments IS A LIST OF `s 91 allotment`
      place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(4) the nominal value of the allotted share capital for paragraph (a)` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `nominal value of the shares in the allotment`)
             (filter (GIVEN a YIELD NOT (`disregarded` a)) allotments))
    WHERE
        `disregarded` a MEANS
                `s 91(2)(b) the allotment may be disregarded` a EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR  (    `s 91(2)(a) the allotment may be disregarded` place a EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 AND (NOT (    `s 91(1)(b) the allotment is paid up as the paragraph requires` a EQUALS JUST TRUE
                           AND `s 91(1)(c) the allotment meets the paragraph` a EQUALS JUST TRUE
                           AND `s 91(1)(d) the allotment meets the paragraph` a EQUALS JUST TRUE)))

-- src:1153 | (5) A company must not be re-registered as a public company if it appears to the registrar that—
-- src:1154 | (a) the company has resolved to reduce its share capital,
-- src:1155 | (b) the reduction—
-- src:1156 | (i) is made under section 626 (reduction in connection with redenomination of share capital),
-- src:1157 | (ii) is supported by a solvency statement in accordance with section 643, or
-- src:1158 | (iii) has been confirmed by an order of the court under section 648, and
-- src:1159 | (c) the effect of the reduction is, or will be, that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is below the authorised minimum.
@ref s 91(5) No re-registration where a reduction takes the capital below the authorised minimum (src:1153-1159)
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar that the company has resolved to reduce its share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 626 the reduction is made under section 626 (redenomination of share capital)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 643 the reduction is supported by a solvency statement in accordance with section 643` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 648 the reduction has been confirmed by an order of the court under section 648` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital after the reduction` IS A NUMBER
      `s 763 the authorised minimum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(5) the company may be re-registered as a public company` MEANS
    IF       `it appears to the registrar that the company has resolved to reduce its share capital`
         AND (    `s 626 the reduction is made under section 626 (redenomination of share capital)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              OR  `s 643 the reduction is supported by a solvency statement in accordance with section 643` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              OR  `s 648 the reduction has been confirmed by an order of the court under section 648` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital after the reduction` BELOW `s 763 the authorised minimum`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must not be re-registered as a public company if it appears to the registrar that"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition names only a company in the position of (a), (b) and (c)

-- ---- s 92: requirements as to net assets ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1160 | 92 Requirements as to net assets
-- src:1161 | (1) A company applying to re-register as a public company must obtain—
-- src:1162 | (a) a balance sheet prepared as at a date not more than seven months before the date on which the application is delivered to the registrar,
@ref s 92(1)(a) A balance sheet prepared as at a date not more than seven months before the application is delivered (src:1160-1162)
GIVEN `the date as at which the balance sheet is prepared` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the application is delivered to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(1)(a) the balance sheet is prepared as at a date not more than seven months before the application is delivered` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the application is delivered to the registrar` AT MOST (`add months` `the date as at which the balance sheet is prepared` 7)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- seven months added to the earlier date, never subtracted from the later one
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a balance sheet prepared as at a date not more than seven months before the date on which the application is delivered to the registrar"

-- src:1170 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (3) a qualification is material unless the auditor states in his report that the matter giving rise to the qualification is not material for the purpose of determining (by reference to the company's balance sheet) whether at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves.
@ref s 92(5) A qualification is material unless the auditor says it is not (src:1170-1170)
GIVEN `the auditor's report contains a qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor states in his report that the matter giving rise to the qualification is not material for the purpose of determining whether at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(5) a qualification is material` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the auditor's report contains a qualification`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a qualification is material unless"; there is no qualification
    ELSE IF `the auditor states in his report that the matter giving rise to the qualification is not material for the purpose of determining whether at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a qualification is material unless the auditor states in his report that the matter giving rise to the qualification is not material"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1166 | (3) In subsection (1)(b) an “unqualified report” means—
-- src:1167 | (a) if the balance sheet was prepared for a financial year of the company, a report stating without material qualification the auditor's opinion that the balance sheet has been properly prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Act;
-- src:1168 | (b) if the balance sheet was not prepared for a financial year of the company, a report stating without material qualification the auditor's opinion that the balance sheet has been properly prepared in accordance with the provisions of this Act which would have applied if it had been prepared for a financial year of the company.
@ref s 92(3) "unqualified report" (src:1166-1168)
GIVEN `the balance sheet was prepared for a financial year of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the auditor's opinion that the balance sheet has been properly prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the auditor's opinion that the balance sheet has been properly prepared in accordance with the provisions of this Act which would have applied if it had been prepared for a financial year of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a qualification in the report is material (s 92(5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(3) the report is an unqualified report` MEANS
    IF `a qualification in the report is material (s 92(5))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a report stating without material qualification the auditor's opinion"
    ELSE IF IF `the balance sheet was prepared for a financial year of the company`
            THEN `the report states the auditor's opinion that the balance sheet has been properly prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Act`
            ELSE `the report states the auditor's opinion that the balance sheet has been properly prepared in accordance with the provisions of this Act which would have applied if it had been prepared for a financial year of the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“unqualified report” means— (a) if the balance sheet was prepared for a financial year of the company, ... (b) if the balance sheet was not prepared for a financial year of the company, ..."

-- src:1160 | 92 Requirements as to net assets
-- src:1161 | (1) A company applying to re-register as a public company must obtain—
-- src:1163 | (b) an unqualified report by the company's auditor on that balance sheet, and
@ref s 92(1)(b) An unqualified report by the auditor on the balance sheet (src:1160-1163)
GIVEN `the company has obtained an auditor's report on the balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 92(3) the report is an unqualified report` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(1)(b) the company has obtained an unqualified report by its auditor on the balance sheet` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has obtained an auditor's report on the balance sheet`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company applying to re-register as a public company must obtain— ... (b) an unqualified report by the company's auditor on that balance sheet"
    ELSE `s 92(3) the report is an unqualified report`

-- src:1164 | (c) a written statement by the company's auditor that in his opinion at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves.
@ref s 92(1)(c) The aggregate of called-up share capital and undistributable reserves (src:1164-1164)
GIVEN `s 547 the amount of the company's called-up share capital` IS A NUMBER
      `s 831 the amount of the company's undistributable reserves` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 92(1)(c) the aggregate of the company's called-up share capital and undistributable reserves` MEANS
    `s 547 the amount of the company's called-up share capital` PLUS `s 831 the amount of the company's undistributable reserves`

-- src:1160 | 92 Requirements as to net assets
-- src:1161 | (1) A company applying to re-register as a public company must obtain—
-- src:1164 | (c) a written statement by the company's auditor that in his opinion at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves.
@ref s 92(1)(c) A written statement by the auditor on net assets (src:1160-1164)
GIVEN `the company has obtained a written statement by its auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that in his opinion at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(1)(c) the company has obtained the auditor's written statement` MEANS
    IF       `the company has obtained a written statement by its auditor`
         AND `the statement says that in his opinion at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company applying to re-register as a public company must obtain— ... (c) a written statement by the company's auditor that in his opinion at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves"

-- src:1165 | (2) Between the balance sheet date and the date on which the application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar, there must be no change in the company's financial position that results in the amount of its net assets becoming less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves.
@ref s 92(2) No change in financial position making net assets less than the aggregate (src:1165-1165)
GIVEN `s 831 the amount of the company's net assets at the balance sheet date` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of called-up share capital and undistributable reserves at the balance sheet date` IS A NUMBER
      `s 831 the amount of the company's net assets on the date the application is delivered` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of called-up share capital and undistributable reserves on the date the application is delivered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(2) there is no change in the company's financial position of the kind the subsection excludes` MEANS
    IF       `s 831 the amount of the company's net assets at the balance sheet date` AT LEAST `the aggregate of called-up share capital and undistributable reserves at the balance sheet date`
         AND `s 831 the amount of the company's net assets on the date the application is delivered` BELOW `the aggregate of called-up share capital and undistributable reserves on the date the application is delivered`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there must be no change in the company's financial position that results in the amount of its net assets becoming less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1169 | (4) For the purposes of an auditor's report on a balance sheet that was not prepared for a financial year of the company, the provisions of this Act apply with such modifications as are necessary by reason of that fact.
@ref s 92(4) An auditor's report on a balance sheet not prepared for a financial year (src:1169-1169)
GIVEN `the auditor's report is on a balance sheet that was not prepared for a financial year of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(4) the provisions of this Act apply to the auditor's report with such modifications as are necessary` MEANS
    IF `the auditor's report is on a balance sheet that was not prepared for a financial year of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- which modifications are "necessary by reason of that fact" is not stated in this Act text: the provisions applying to a report for a financial year are read with them
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of an auditor's report on a balance sheet that was not prepared for a financial year of the company"

-- src:1171 | (6) In this Part “net assets” and “undistributable reserves” have the same meaning as in section 831 (net asset restriction on distributions by public companies).
@ref s 92(6) "net assets" and "undistributable reserves" (src:1171-1171)
GIVEN `s 831 the amount worked out as section 831 provides` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 92(6) the amount of the company's net assets or undistributable reserves` MEANS
    `s 831 the amount worked out as section 831 provides` -- "have the same meaning as in section 831": the meaning is another part's (points outside the text), so the figure is taken as an input

-- src:1160 | 92 Requirements as to net assets
-- src:1161 | (1) A company applying to re-register as a public company must obtain—
-- src:1162 | (a) a balance sheet prepared as at a date not more than seven months before the date on which the application is delivered to the registrar,
-- src:1163 | (b) an unqualified report by the company's auditor on that balance sheet, and
-- src:1164 | (c) a written statement by the company's auditor that in his opinion at the balance sheet date the amount of the company's net assets was not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves.
-- src:1165 | (2) Between the balance sheet date and the date on which the application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar, there must be no change in the company's financial position that results in the amount of its net assets becoming less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves.
@ref s 92(1) Requirements as to net assets (together) (src:1160-1165)
GIVEN `s 92(1)(a) the balance sheet is prepared as at a date not more than seven months before the application is delivered` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 92(1)(b) the company has obtained an unqualified report by its auditor on the balance sheet` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 92(1)(c) the company has obtained the auditor's written statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 92(2) there is no change in the company's financial position of the kind the subsection excludes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92 the requirements as to net assets are met` MEANS
    `s 90(1) all of the answers hold`
        (LIST `s 92(1)(a) the balance sheet is prepared as at a date not more than seven months before the application is delivered`
            , `s 92(1)(b) the company has obtained an unqualified report by its auditor on the balance sheet`
            , `s 92(1)(c) the company has obtained the auditor's written statement`
            , `s 92(2) there is no change in the company's financial position of the kind the subsection excludes`)

-- ---- s 93: recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration -----------------------------------------

-- src:1172 | 93 Recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration
-- src:1173 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:1174 | (a) shares are allotted by the company in the period between the date as at which the balance sheet required by section 92 is prepared and the passing of the resolution that the company should re-register as a public company, and
-- src:1175 | (b) the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up as to their nominal value or any premium on them otherwise than in cash.
@ref s 93(1) Where the section applies (src:1172-1175)
GIVEN `shares are allotted by the company in the period between the date as at which the balance sheet required by section 92 is prepared and the passing of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up as to their nominal value or any premium on those shares otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(1) section 93 applies (recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration)` MEANS
    IF       `shares are allotted by the company in the period between the date as at which the balance sheet required by section 92 is prepared and the passing of the resolution`
         AND `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up as to their nominal value or any premium on those shares otherwise than in cash`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) ... and (b) ..."

-- src:1197 | (b) “arrangement” means any agreement, scheme or arrangement, (including an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with—
-- src:1198 | (i) Part 26 or 26A of this Act (arrangements and reconstructions), or
-- src:1199 | (ii) section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)) (liquidator in winding up accepting shares as consideration for sale of company's property)).
@ref s 93(7)(b) "arrangement" (src:1197-1199)
GIVEN `it is an agreement, scheme or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26 or 26A of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an arrangement under section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(7)(b) the thing is an arrangement` MEANS
    IF       `it is an agreement, scheme or arrangement`
         OR  `it is an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26 or 26A of this Act`
         OR  `it is an arrangement under section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“arrangement” means any agreement, scheme or arrangement, (including an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with— (i) ..., (ii) ...)"

-- src:1186 | (4) In determining whether a person is a holder of shares for the purposes of subsection (3), there shall be disregarded—
-- src:1187 | (a) shares held by, or by a nominee of, the company allotting the shares;
-- src:1188 | (b) shares held by, or by a nominee of—
-- src:1189 | (i) the holding company of the company allotting the shares,
-- src:1190 | (ii) a subsidiary of the company allotting the shares, or
-- src:1191 | (iii) a subsidiary of the holding company of the company allotting the shares.
@ref s 93(4) Holders whose shares are disregarded (src:1186-1191)
GIVEN `the shares are held by, or by a nominee of, the company allotting the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held by, or by a nominee of, the holding company of the company allotting the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held by, or by a nominee of, a subsidiary of the company allotting the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held by, or by a nominee of, a subsidiary of the holding company of the company allotting the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(4) the shares are disregarded in determining whether a person is a holder of shares` MEANS
    IF       `the shares are held by, or by a nominee of, the company allotting the shares`
         OR  `the shares are held by, or by a nominee of, the holding company of the company allotting the shares`
         OR  `the shares are held by, or by a nominee of, a subsidiary of the company allotting the shares`
         OR  `the shares are held by, or by a nominee of, a subsidiary of the holding company of the company allotting the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "there shall be disregarded" names four kinds of holding and does not say that no other is disregarded

-- src:1181 | (3) An allotment is in connection with a share exchange if—
-- src:1182 | (a) the shares are allotted in connection with an arrangement under which the whole or part of the consideration for the shares allotted is provided by—
-- src:1183 | (i) the transfer to the company allotting the shares of shares (or shares of a particular class) in another company, or
-- src:1184 | (ii) the cancellation of shares (or shares of a particular class) in another company; and
-- src:1185 | (b) the allotment is open to all the holders of the shares of the other company in question (or, where the arrangement applies only to shares of a particular class, to all the holders of the company's shares of that class) to take part in the arrangement in connection with which the shares are allotted.
@ref s 93(3) An allotment in connection with a share exchange (src:1181-1185)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted in connection with an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the whole or part of the consideration is provided by the transfer to the company allotting the shares of shares (or shares of a particular class) in another company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the whole or part of the consideration is provided by the cancellation of shares (or shares of a particular class) in another company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is open to all the holders of the shares of the other company in question (or, where the arrangement applies only to shares of a particular class, to all the holders of the company's shares of that class) to take part in the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(3) the allotment is in connection with a share exchange` MEANS
    IF       `the shares are allotted in connection with an arrangement`
         AND (    `the whole or part of the consideration is provided by the transfer to the company allotting the shares of shares (or shares of a particular class) in another company`
              OR  `the whole or part of the consideration is provided by the cancellation of shares (or shares of a particular class) in another company`)
         AND `the allotment is open to all the holders of the shares of the other company in question (or, where the arrangement applies only to shares of a particular class, to all the holders of the company's shares of that class) to take part in the arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An allotment is in connection with a share exchange if— (a) ... and (b) ..."

-- src:1192 | (5) It is immaterial, for the purposes of deciding whether an allotment is in connection with a share exchange, whether or not the arrangement in connection with which the shares are allotted involves the issue to the company allotting the shares of shares (or shares of a particular class) in the other company.
@ref s 93(5) Whether the arrangement involves an issue of shares in the other company is immaterial (src:1192-1192)
GIVEN `the arrangement involves the issue to the company allotting the shares of shares (or shares of a particular class) in the other company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(5) it matters whether the arrangement involves an issue of shares in the other company` MEANS
    IF `the arrangement involves the issue to the company allotting the shares of shares (or shares of a particular class) in the other company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial, for the purposes of deciding whether an allotment is in connection with a share exchange, whether or not the arrangement ... involves the issue to the company allotting the shares of shares ... in the other company"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial ... whether or not the arrangement ... involves the issue"

-- src:1193 | (6) There is a proposed merger with another company if one of the companies concerned proposes to acquire all the assets and liabilities of the other in exchange for the issue of its shares or other securities to shareholders of the other (whether or not accompanied by a cash payment).
@ref s 93(6) A proposed merger (src:1193-1193)
GIVEN `one of the companies concerned proposes to acquire all the assets and liabilities of the other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in exchange for the issue of its shares or other securities to shareholders of the other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exchange is accompanied by a cash payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(6) there is a proposed merger with another company` MEANS
    IF       `one of the companies concerned proposes to acquire all the assets and liabilities of the other`
         AND `in exchange for the issue of its shares or other securities to shareholders of the other`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whether or not accompanied by a cash payment: `the exchange is accompanied by a cash payment` is not read
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "There is a proposed merger with another company if one of the companies concerned proposes to acquire all the assets and liabilities of the other in exchange for the issue of its shares or other securities to shareholders of the other"

-- src:1194 | “Another company” includes any body corporate.
@ref s 93(6) "Another company" includes any body corporate (src:1194-1194)
GIVEN `it is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(6) the body is another company` MEANS
    IF `it is a body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Another company” includes any body corporate"

-- src:1195 | (7) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:1196 | (a) the consideration for an allotment does not include any amount standing to the credit of any of the company's reserve accounts, or of its profit and loss account, that has been applied in paying up (to any extent) any of the shares allotted or any premium on those shares; and
@ref s 93(7)(a) Reserves applied in paying up shares are not consideration (src:1195-1196)
GIVEN `the amount stands to the credit of one of the company's reserve accounts, or of its profit and loss account, and has been applied in paying up (to any extent) any of the shares allotted or any premium on those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(7)(a) the amount counts as consideration for the allotment` MEANS
    IF `the amount stands to the credit of one of the company's reserve accounts, or of its profit and loss account, and has been applied in paying up (to any extent) any of the shares allotted or any premium on those shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the consideration for an allotment does not include any amount standing to the credit of any of the company's reserve accounts, or of its profit and loss account, that has been applied in paying up"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names only amounts standing to the credit of reserve accounts or the profit and loss account that have been applied in paying up shares

-- src:1176 | (2) The registrar shall not entertain an application by the company for re-registration as a public company unless—
-- src:1177 | (a) the requirements of section 593(1)(a) and (b) have been complied with (independent valuation of non-cash consideration; valuer's report to company not more than six months before allotment), or
-- src:1178 | (b) the allotment is in connection with—
-- src:1179 | (i) a share exchange (see subsections (3) to (5) below), or
-- src:1180 | (ii) a proposed merger with another company (see subsection (6) below).
@ref s 93(2) The registrar shall not entertain the application unless (src:1176-1180)
GIVEN `s 93(1) section 93 applies (recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 593(1) the requirements of paragraphs (a) and (b) of section 593(1) have been complied with` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 93(3) the allotment is in connection with a share exchange` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 93(6) there is a proposed merger with another company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(2) the registrar may entertain the application for re-registration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 93(1) section 93 applies (recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       `s 593(1) the requirements of paragraphs (a) and (b) of section 593(1) have been complied with` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR  `s 93(3) the allotment is in connection with a share exchange` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR  `s 93(6) there is a proposed merger with another company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE -- the "unless" is met: the bar lifts (fork 5)
        ELSE IF       `s 593(1) the requirements of paragraphs (a) and (b) of section 593(1) have been complied with` EQUALS NOTHING
                  OR  `s 93(3) the allotment is in connection with a share exchange` EQUALS NOTHING
                  OR  `s 93(6) there is a proposed merger with another company` EQUALS NOTHING
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 593(1) is another part's answer and it is not known
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar shall not entertain an application by the company for re-registration as a public company unless"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 93 applies only where shares were recently allotted for non-cash consideration
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 93 applies is not known

-- ---- s 94: application and accompanying documents -----------------------------------------------------

-- src:1200 | 94 Application and accompanying documents
-- src:1201 | (1) An application for re-registration as a public company must contain—
-- src:1202 | (a) a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration; and
-- src:1203 | (b) in the case of a company without a secretary, a statement of the company's proposed secretary (see section 95).
@ref s 94(1) The application must contain (src:1200-1203)
GIVEN `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is without a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(1) the application contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration`
         AND (    (NOT (`the company is without a secretary`))
              OR  `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed secretary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- (b) is required only "in the case of a company without a secretary"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application for re-registration as a public company must contain— (a) a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration; and (b) in the case of a company without a secretary, a statement of the company's proposed secretary"

-- src:1200 | 94 Application and accompanying documents
-- src:1204 | (2) The application must be accompanied by—
-- src:1205 | (a) a copy of the special resolution that the company should re-register as a public company (unless a copy has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3);
-- src:1206 | (b) a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended;
-- src:1207 | (c) a copy of the balance sheet and other documents referred to in section 92(1); ...
-- src:1208 | (d) if section 93 applies (recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration), a copy of the valuation report (if any) under subsection (2)(a) of that section; and
-- src:1209 | (e) a statement of the aggregate amount paid up on the shares of the company on account of their nominal value.
@ref s 94(2) The application must be accompanied by (src:1200-1209)
GIVEN `a copy of the special resolution that the company should re-register as a public company accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of that resolution has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the balance sheet and other documents referred to in section 92(1) accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 93 applies and a valuation report under section 93(2)(a) exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the valuation report accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of the aggregate amount paid up on the shares of the company on account of their nominal value accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(2) the application is accompanied by what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       (`a copy of the special resolution that the company should re-register as a public company accompanies the application` OR `a copy of that resolution has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3`)
         AND `a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompanies the application`
         AND `a copy of the balance sheet and other documents referred to in section 92(1) accompanies the application`
         AND (    (NOT (`section 93 applies and a valuation report under section 93(2)(a) exists`))
              OR  `a copy of the valuation report accompanies the application`)
         AND `a statement of the aggregate amount paid up on the shares of the company on account of their nominal value accompanies the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be accompanied by— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ... (e) ..."

-- src:1210 | (3) The statement of compliance required to be delivered together with the application is a statement that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a public company have been complied with.
@ref s 94(3) The statement of compliance (src:1210-1210)
GIVEN `the statement is that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a public company have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(3) the statement meets the description of the statement of compliance` MEANS
    IF `the statement is that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a public company have been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of compliance ... is a statement that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a public company have been complied with."

-- src:1211 | (4) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a public company.
@ref s 94(4) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance (src:1211-1211)
GIVEN `a statement of compliance has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(4) the registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a public company` MEANS
    IF `a statement of compliance has been delivered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may accept the statement of compliance"; there is none

-- ---- s 95: statement of proposed secretary ---------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 95(2) kind of proposed secretary` IS ONE OF
    `s 95(2) an individual`
    `s 95(2) a corporate secretary or a firm`

-- src:1212 | 95 Statement of proposed secretary
-- src:1213 | (1) The statement of the company's proposed secretary must contain the required information about the person who is or the persons who are to be the secretary or joint secretaries of the company.
-- src:1214 | (2) For the required information in relation to proposed secretaries or joint secretaries, see sections 279J and 279K.
@ref s 95(1) The statement must contain the required information (src:1212-1214)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 95(2) kind of proposed secretary`
      `s 279J the statement contains the required information about the individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 279K the statement contains the required information about the corporate secretary or firm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(1) the statement of the company's proposed secretary contains the required information` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 95(2) an individual` THEN `s 279J the statement contains the required information about the individual`
    WHEN `s 95(2) a corporate secretary or a firm` THEN `s 279K the statement contains the required information about the corporate secretary or firm`

-- src:1212 | 95 Statement of proposed secretary
-- src:1215 | (3) The statement must also include a statement by the company that the person named as secretary, or each of the persons named as joint secretaries, has consented to act in the relevant capacity.
@ref s 95(3) The statement must include the company's statement that the secretary has consented to act (src:1212-1215)
GIVEN `the statement includes a statement by the company that the person named as secretary, or each of the persons named as joint secretaries, has consented to act in the relevant capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(3) the statement of the proposed secretary includes the company's statement of consent` MEANS
    IF `the statement includes a statement by the company that the person named as secretary, or each of the persons named as joint secretaries, has consented to act in the relevant capacity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement must also include a statement by the company that the person named as secretary, or each of the persons named as joint secretaries, has consented to act in the relevant capacity."

-- src:1212 | 95 Statement of proposed secretary
-- src:1216 | If all the partners in a firm are to be joint secretaries, consent may be given by one partner on behalf of all of them.
@ref s 95(3) Consent by one partner on behalf of all (src:1212-1216)
GIVEN `all the partners in a firm are to be joint secretaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `consent is given by one partner on behalf of all of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(3) consent may be given by one partner on behalf of all of them` MEANS
    IF `all the partners in a firm are to be joint secretaries` AND `consent is given by one partner on behalf of all of them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If all the partners in a firm are to be joint secretaries, consent may be given by one partner on behalf of all of them."

-- ---- s 96: issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration -----------------------------------

-- src:1217 | 96 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1218 | (1) If on an application for re-registration as a public company the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered, the company shall be re-registered accordingly.
@ref s 96(1) The company shall be re-registered (src:1217-1218)
GIVEN `the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1) the company shall be re-registered as a public company` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application for re-registration as a public company the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered, the company shall be re-registered accordingly."

-- src:1217 | 96 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1219 | (2) The registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 96(2) The registrar must issue a certificate (src:1217-1219)
GIVEN `the company has been re-registered under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(2) the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case` MEANS
    IF `the company has been re-registered under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty follows the re-registration of subsection (1)

-- src:1217 | 96 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1220 | (3) The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is issued.
@ref s 96(3) What the certificate must state (src:1217-1220)
GIVEN `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states the date on which it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(3) the certificate meets the requirement of subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` AND `the certificate states the date on which it is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is issued."

-- src:1217 | 96 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1221 | (4) On the issue of the certificate—
-- src:1222 | (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes a public company,
@ref s 96(4)(a) The company becomes a public company on the issue of the certificate (src:1217-1222)
GIVEN `the date on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(4)(a) the company is a public company on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the certificate is issued`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes a public company" (no certificate has been issued)
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF day AT LEAST issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes a public company"

-- src:1217 | 96 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1221 | (4) On the issue of the certificate—
-- src:1223 | (b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect, and
@ref s 96(4)(b) The changes in the company's name and articles take effect (src:1217-1223)
GIVEN `the date on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(4)(b) the changes in the company's name and articles have taken effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the certificate is issued`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— ... (b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect" (no certificate has been issued)
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF day AT LEAST issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— ... (b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect"

-- src:1217 | 96 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1221 | (4) On the issue of the certificate—
-- src:1224 | (c) where the application contained a statement under section 95 (statement of proposed secretary), the person or persons named in the statement as secretary or joint secretary of the company are deemed to have been appointed to that office.
@ref s 96(4)(c) A proposed secretary is deemed appointed (src:1217-1224)
GIVEN `the application contained a statement under section 95 (statement of proposed secretary)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(4)(c) the person named in the statement as secretary is deemed to have been appointed on the day` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application contained a statement under section 95 (statement of proposed secretary)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the application contained a statement under section 95"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date on which the certificate is issued`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— ... (c) ... the person or persons named in the statement as secretary or joint secretary of the company are deemed to have been appointed to that office" (no certificate has been issued)
         WHEN JUST issued THEN
             IF day AT LEAST issued
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— ... (c) ... deemed to have been appointed to that office"

-- src:1217 | 96 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1225 | (5) The certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Act as to re-registration have been complied with.
@ref s 96(5) The certificate is conclusive evidence (src:1217-1225)
GIVEN `a certificate has been issued on the re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(5) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Act as to re-registration have been complied with` MEANS
    IF `a certificate has been issued on the re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The certificate is conclusive evidence"; there is no certificate

